From: Flax Advisors <support@flaxadvisors.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] redfish: render PCIeDevice.FirmwareVersion

The Redfish PCIeDevice schema carries FirmwareVersion, but bmcweb never
populated it -- pcie.hpp contains no reference to a version at all.  The TP26
BIOS reports adapter firmware over the host interface for cards that have one
(the Mellanox ConnectX-4 Lx gives 14.27.26.06), so the data reached the BMC and
then had nowhere to go.

Read it from Decorator.Revision, which is the interface bmcweb already uses for
a processor's Version and which flax-hi-inventory now publishes on PCIe device
objects.  Absent on devices with no known firmware, which is most of them, and
that is not an error.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp
index 83a0912..7368cb2 100644
--- a/redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp
@@ -335,6 +335,34 @@ inline void getPCIeDeviceState(
         });
 }
 
+// Adapter firmware, where the producer knows it.  The Redfish PCIeDevice
+// schema carries FirmwareVersion but bmcweb never populated it; the TP26 BIOS
+// reports it over the host interface for cards that have one (the Mellanox
+// ConnectX-4 Lx gives 14.27.26.06), and flax-hi-inventory publishes it on
+// Decorator.Revision -- the same interface bmcweb already reads for a
+// processor's Version.
+inline void getPCIeDeviceRevision(
+    const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
+    const std::string& pcieDevicePath, const std::string& service)
+{
+    dbus::utility::getProperty<std::string>(
+        service, pcieDevicePath,
+        "xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Revision", "Version",
+        [asyncResp](const boost::system::error_code& ec,
+                    const std::string& version) {
+            if (ec)
+            {
+                // Absent on devices whose firmware version is unknown, which
+                // is most of them.  Not an error.
+                return;
+            }
+            if (!version.empty())
+            {
+                asyncResp->res.jsonValue["FirmwareVersion"] = version;
+            }
+        });
+}
+
 inline void getPCIeDeviceAsset(
     const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
     const std::string& pcieDevicePath, const std::string& service)
@@ -545,6 +573,7 @@ inline void afterGetValidPcieDevicePath(
 {
     addPCIeDeviceCommonProperties(asyncResp, pcieDeviceId);
     getPCIeDeviceAsset(asyncResp, pcieDevicePath, service);
+    getPCIeDeviceRevision(asyncResp, pcieDevicePath, service);
     getPCIeDeviceState(asyncResp, pcieDevicePath, service);
     getPCIeDeviceHealth(asyncResp, pcieDevicePath, service);
     getPCIeDeviceProperties(
